      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I am pretty sure I found out why this happens:\n\n- Make a project with the avatar\n\n- Upload the PC version\n\n- Upload the Quest version\n\n- Says \"upload succeeded\", but the Quest version is not uploaded, the platform Android does not appear in the Supported Platforms\n\n- Close the project\n\n- Open the project again from the CC\n\n- Upload the Quest version\n\n- Now it says the avatar is over the 10mb limit\n\n- Change it so the avatar is under the 10mb limit'\n\n- Upload the Quest version\n\n- Says \"upload succeeded\", the platform Android appears in the Supported Platforms\n\nI suspect it is due to the migration From 2019 to 2022, because avatars take more space in the 2022 version. Meaning this avatar was migrated from a 2019 package to a 2022 package. \n\nThis filesize change seems to apply to all avatars, at least the Quest avatars take more space.\n\nThe question is why do you have to restart Unity for the SDK itself to notice.. I think the server notices and it declines the upload because of the filesize being more than 10mb, but the SDK does not see it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
